# Two things fixed here (2026-07-18):
#
# 1. Every legacy-alias rule below now has a matching trailing-slash
#    variant too — Cloudflare Pages/Netlify _redirects matching is
#    literal, so "/about-us" does NOT also match "/about-us/". Without
#    the second copy, a trailing-slash visit (very common from old
#    WordPress links/bookmarks, which canonicalize with a trailing slash
#    by default) fell through to the SPA with no matching React Router
#    route and rendered blank — this is exactly the reported /about-us/
#    bug. App.js also has a catch-all route to Home as a last-resort
#    safety net for anything not listed here.
#
# 2. Removed 3 rules that were silently hijacking real, dedicated React
#    pages: /calculators, /services, and /contact all have their own
#    proper page component (CalculatorsPage, ServicesPage, ContactPage)
#    registered in App.js, but the old rules below were redirecting them
#    to a hash-anchor section on the homepage instead (/#calculators,
#    /#services, /#contact) before they ever reached the real page —
#    likely left over from before those dedicated pages existed. The
#    hash-anchor aliases (/mutual-funds, /calculator, /contact-us, etc.)
#    that don't collide with a real route are untouched.

